index 0000000..99d294a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/_models/sbm.html
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+layout: post
+title: "Stochastic Block Model (SBM)"
+summary: "Community detection in a random graph with a planted partition."
+---
+<!--
+  A model page: the setup once, then the results you keep needing.
+  Give each result an id="..." so posts can link straight to it,
+  e.g. <a href="/models/sbm/#kesten-stigum">Kesten–Stigum threshold</a>.
+  Example entries below; check them against your sources.
+-->
+
+<h2>Setup</h2>
+<p>Two balanced communities: assign each vertex $i \in [n]$ a label $\sigma_i \in \{\pm 1\}$ uniformly at random. Connect $i$ and $j$ independently with probability $a/n$ if $\sigma_i = \sigma_j$ and $b/n$ otherwise. Goal: recover $\sigma$ from the graph, up to a global sign.</p>
+<p><em>Weak recovery</em> means outputting $\hat\sigma$ with overlap $\big|\tfrac1n \sum_i \hat\sigma_i \sigma_i\big| \ge \delta$ for some $\delta > 0$, with probability $1 - o(1)$.</p>
+
+<h2>Results</h2>
+
+<div class="box theorem" id="kesten-stigum">
+  <div class="box-title">Kesten–Stigum threshold</div>
+  <p class="statement">Weak recovery is possible if and only if $(a-b)^2 > 2(a+b)$.</p>
+  <p>Equivalently, with $a = d(1+\varepsilon)$, $b = d(1-\varepsilon)$ and $\lambda = \varepsilon\sqrt d$: weak recovery is possible if and only if $\lambda > 1$.</p>
+  <p class="source">Mossel–Neeman–Sly (impossibility below); Massoulié and Mossel–Neeman–Sly (algorithms above).</p>
+</div>
+
+<h2>Open questions / my notes</h2>
+<p>…</p>
diff --git a/_models/sk.html b/_models/sk.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8fb530
--- /dev/null
+++ b/_models/sk.html
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+layout: post
+title: "Sherrington–Kirkpatrick Model (SK)"
+summary: "Mean-field spin glass with i.i.d. Gaussian couplings."
+---
+<!--
+  Example entries below; check them against your sources.
+-->
+
+<h2>Setup</h2>
+<p>For $\sigma \in \{\pm 1\}^n$ and i.i.d. couplings $g_{ij} \sim \mathcal N(0,1)$, the Gibbs measure at inverse temperature $\beta$ is
+$$ \mu_\beta(\sigma) \propto \exp\Big( \frac{\beta}{\sqrt n} \sum_{i<j} g_{ij}\, \sigma_i \sigma_j \Big). $$</p>
+
+<h2>Results</h2>
+
+<div class="box theorem" id="parisi-formula">
+  <div class="box-title">Parisi formula</div>
+  <p class="statement">The limiting free energy $\lim_{n\to\infty} \tfrac1n \E \log Z_n(\beta)$ exists and equals the infimum of the Parisi functional.</p>
+  <p class="source">Guerra (upper bound); Talagrand, 2006.</p>
+</div>
+
+<div class="box theorem" id="glauber-high-temp">
+  <div class="box-title">Fast mixing of Glauber at high temperature</div>
+  <p class="statement">For $\beta < 1/4$, Glauber dynamics has spectral gap $\Omega(1/n)$ with high probability over the couplings.</p>
+  <p class="source">Eldan–Koehler–Zeitouni.</p>
+</div>
+
+<h2>Open questions / my notes</h2>
+<p>…</p>
